    98	## Global Constraints
    99	
   100	- Toolchain and Mathlib v4.30.0-rc2. Do not run `lake update`.
   101	- No `sorry`, `admit`, `native_decide`, or new axioms. Allowed axioms: `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.
   102	- The Mac `lean` is a throttle wrapper (3 slots). Run `pgrep -fl lean` before a build. Use `lake env lean --run <file>` for scripts; never a `lean_exe`.
   103	- Do not edit `AvailableChainStatements/**` or `AvailableChainModel/**`.
   104	- Do not change the statement of `gridContract_from_engine`, `saContract_from_engine`, `sapcContract_from_engine`, `sapcStrong_from_engine`, or of any theorem that `AvailableChainSA/Tests/Axioms.lean` or `AvailableChainSAPC/Tests/Axioms.lean` prints. A statement change elsewhere in a protocol library is allowed only to add the "not excluded at the deadline" premise of Task 1 and must be listed in the task report.
   105	- The FG-SA constraint above: no change to the bodies of `admitProposal`, `admitVote`, `gate`, `propose`, the voter views; no change to the statements of `gate_target_origin`, `confirmation_mem`, `gate_eq_writeKeys`, `admitVote_*`, `gate_blocks`, `recordGenuine`; no move of `AvailableChainGridCO.Proofs.{GenuineHistory, History, Map, RecordSlots, Roots}`.
   106	- The catalog lock: `CatalogLock --check` exits 0 after every task, with no CHANGED or REMOVED line. Task 4 adds lines with `--write` (no `--allow-changes`).
   107	- Registry: `scripts/Registry.lean` then `--check` exit 0 after every task that changes the Registry library.
   108	- `bash scripts/check-fg.sh` exits 0 at Tasks 0 and 7 (the Kit move changes GridCO imports; KitFG must still build).
   109	- Commit by explicit path. Never stage `log.md`, `state.md`, `docs/FG-COMPOSITION.md`. Commit messages end with the `Claude-Session:` line.
   110	- Prose in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English; tables in Unicode box drawing inside fenced `text` blocks.
   111	
   112	## Review Focus
   113	
   114	1. **`excludes` must not over-exclude.** An object that `admitVote` would still accept later must never be excluded. Otherwise `PartialSynchrony` drops a real delivery obligation, and the regime admits runs in which a still-acceptable HEAD is never delivered; the proofs would then fail or, worse, a later weaker proof would certify those runs. Test: in Task 1, `excludes_head_iff` (both directions) and `excludes_proposal`, plus the stability of exclusion (`excludes_stable`), which shows the refusal is permanent.
   115	2. **A HEAD accepted in the last Δ before its exclusion time.** A relay lemma that concludes a handler call at the reader for such a HEAD is now false. Every such lemma gets the premise; no caller may discharge it for a label-`r` HEAD with a deadline after `proposalTime (r + 2)`.
   116	3. **A third HEAD from an equivocating faulty seat** is excluded at any time. A caller that relays a faulty HEAD must accept the "`∨ equivocates`" outcome (as `accepted_head_receipt_before` already does, `ReceiptRelay.lean:133-160`), or prove non-equivocation.
   117	4. **`processed` and `excludes` stay disjoint** after every step of a run, not only in one state.
   118	5. **The Kit move changes no statement.** Every moved declaration keeps its name and namespace; `git diff -M` shows moves, and a name-by-name check of `#print axioms` for the moved theorems passes.
   119	
