   285	## 4. Claim catalog (L3)
   286	
   287	```lean
   288	structure ClaimSpec where
   289	  id        : Lean.Name
   290	  needs     : FacetNeeds
   291	  Const     : Type                           -- this claim's constants
   292	  valid     : Const → Prop
   293	  le        : Const → Const → Bool           -- decidable; `le c c'`: c' is
   294	                                             -- at least as weak as c
   295	  le_refl   : ∀ c, le c c
   296	  le_trans  : ∀ a b c, le a b → le b c → le a c
   297	  holds     : Instance → Const → Prop
   298	  transport : ∀ I c c', valid c → valid c' → le c c' →
   299	                holds I c → holds I c'
   300	  trigger   : Instance → Const → Run → Prop  -- the claim's trigger occurs
   301	                                             -- with its deadline in the run
   302	  inhabited : Instance → Const → Prop        -- §5
   303	  refutable : RefutationKind
   304	```
   305	
   306	- Per-parameter behaviour (audit tables): the claim is weaker when θ ↑,
   307	  θrec ↑, η ↑, A ↑, A_f ↑, ρ ↑, recoveryFull false → true, G ↓, Π ↓,
   308	  faultCap ↓, and D ↑ for persistent inclusion. Exact-time inclusion is
   309	  `fixed` in D: its `le` is equality on D.
   310	- `transport` is a proof, not metadata. Composite comparisons compose
   311	  transports; `le_refl` and `le_trans` make that sound.
   312	- Relation lemmas may combine certificates of ONE instance and require
   313	  equal values for their shared constants. Example:
   314	  `Safe o ∧ included o D ⇒ includedPersist o D` (same D). `Safe o` is one
   315	  conjunction: agreement and per-node monotonicity, as today's `SafeFrom`.
   316	- `includedPersist o D` (B is in every honest read of `o` at every time
   317	  from `s + D` to the horizon) is a DERIVED lemma in `Kit.Core`, not a
   318	  catalog entry: every instance is safe (core floor), so it follows from
   319	  `Safe o` and `included o D` (user decision 2026-09-28).
   320	- Regimes with a minimum horizon (Outage b₁, Recovery GST + ρ, StrongArmed
   321	  b₀) are closed under complete time truncation only above it. Causal
   322	  arguments use separate EXECUTION-PREFIX predicates (L1), not the
   323	  complete-run regimes; an event-list prefix inside one time can break
   324	  `tick_total`.
   325	
   326	**Profiles.** A profile is a set of catalog ids plus shared constant
   327	names. A profile certificate is a set of certificates of one instance
   328	that agree on the shared constants. `ac-4.3` is today's bundle: the
   329	equivalence is between claim PROPOSITIONS (`AvailableChain ↔` the
   330	conjunction of the `ac-4.3` `holds`). Eligibility (hooks,
   331	deliverability, inhabitation) is separate, because `AvailableChain`
   332	contains none of it (V07). `strong-1` is `StrongClaims`.
   333	
   334	Tiers:
   335	
   336	```text
   337	┌──────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   338	│ Tier         │ Entries                                               │
   339	├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
   340	│ core (floor) │ Safe(confirmed), Safe(stable), prefix(stable ⪯        │
   341	│              │ confirmed), included(confirmed) under Sleepy          │
   342	│ standard     │ included(stable) under StableSleepy, fast             │
   343	│              │ inclusion, persistence (general, fast), recovered     │
   344	│              │ variants                                              │
   345	│ extra        │ strong claims; base exports; P1 from a recovered      │
   346	│              │ handoff; noFutureRead; catchUp; later additions       │
   347	│ fg-ready     │ AP-side FG entries (FG-COMPOSITION.md)                │
   348	│ composite    │ derived by Kit.Compose (FG-COMPOSITION.md)            │
   349	└──────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   350	```
   351	
   352	The core is a FLOOR (user decision 2026-09-28): an instance is a
   353	candidate protocol only if it certifies every core claim. A refutation
   354	of a core claim rejects the instance. Selection of claims ("all but
   355	one", optional extras) applies only above the core. The explorer and
   356	the Pareto comparison consider only instances that pass the floor.
   357	Unsafe or not-live protocols are out of scope.
   358	
   359	**As implemented in plan 1a (2026-09-28).** This note does not change
   360	the text above. `ClaimSpec K` is generic over a claim domain `K` and has
   361	no `needs` field. `holds` and `inhabited` are definitions over the
   362	fields `regime`, `conclusion` and `trigger`. The trigger takes a time
   363	`H`, and `inhabited` needs the trigger at a time of at least `H` (the
   364	late trigger; I2 in §12). The type does not force this, so each claim
   365	with a trigger other than `True` proves `<claim>_trigger_late`. A
   366	profile has a type of shared constants `Profile.Shared`, and each entry
   367	projects the shared constant to the constant of its claim
   368	(`Profile.Entry.share`). `Profile.valid` holds the conditions between
   369	the constants of different claims. `ac-4.3` (`ac43` in
   370	`Catalog/Profiles.lean`) has `Shared := Constants` and nine claims;
   371	`ac43_iff` is its proposition equivalence with `AvailableChain`.
   372	`strong-1` (`strong1`) has `Shared := Constants × StrongConstants` and
   373	five claims over the strong claim domain; `strong1_iff` is its
   374	equivalence with `StrongClaims`. The standard tier is in
   375	`Catalog/Standard.lean`, the strong claims are in `Catalog/Strong.lean`,
   376	and the core floor is `core` in `Catalog/Core.lean` (`Shared := Time`,
   377	the D of confirmed inclusion).
   378	
   379	## 5. Certificates, refutations, registry (L4, L6)
   380	
   381	```lean
   382	structure Cert (c : ClaimSpec) (I : Instance) where
   383	  const     : c.Const
   384	  valid     : c.valid const
   385	  inhabited : c.inhabited I const
   386	  proof     : c.holds I const
   387	
   388	structure Refutation (c : ClaimSpec) (I : Instance) where
   389	  const     : c.Const
   390	  valid     : c.valid const
   391	  proof     : ¬ c.holds I const
   392	```
   393	
   394	**Inhabitation (V07).** `inhabited I c`: for every horizon H there is a
   395	run of I in the claim's regime, with horizon ≥ H, in which the claim's
   396	TRIGGER occurs with its deadline inside the run: for inclusion, an
   397	honest awake proposer slot; for persistence, a non-genesis armed read;
   398	for FG entries, a nonempty source. Boundary cases are allowed (no fault
   399	when the regime forbids one). `Kit.Engine` supplies the runs through the
   400	run-extension theorem (E4). Transport of `holds` does not transport
   401	`inhabited`.
   402	
   403	**Refutations.** Finite runs for bounded claims; parameterized finite
   404	families for "no constant works" (as the Sanity theorem does for every
   405	D). Kernel checking with `decide_cbv` or a reflective checker whose
   406	soundness covers the execution, the regime and the failed conclusion;
   407	`native_decide` is not allowed. Executable checkers exist only for
   408	instances with finite representations and equivalence proofs.
   409	
   410	**Registry.** Checked attributes (`@[cert]`, `@[refutes]`) verify the
   411	elaborated type, including instance and constants; a theorem with extra
   412	unproved premises is not a certificate. Per instance and claim the
   413	registry keeps the Pareto set of proved constants, the refuted
   414	constants, the proof status (Lean certificate, paper, conditional),
   415	assumptions, output names and module versions. A paper result never
   416	appears as a Lean certificate.
   417	
   418	**Freeze.** `catalog.lock`: per L1, LM, L2, L3 declaration, a
   419	deterministic hash of the transitive dependency closure (types, bodies,
   420	inductives, opaque bodies via `getUsedConstantsAsSet`; fail if a body is
   421	unavailable). Per L0 and LM version, a frozen content hash. The
   422	toolchain and Lake manifest are pinned. Each certificate records its
   423	instance, constants and dependency hashes. The freeze is syntactic; it
   424	does not replace kernel checking.
   425	
