/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:3:The recommended first change is to keep the raw `Block` type and the generic `RootInjective` premise, fix the three proposer implementations, and add a root check to both block admission and proposal wire validity. Then prove `RootInjective` for every `ExecutionValid` run of each fixed protocol. This removes the extra root assumption from applications of those protocols without changing the generic catalog. A check in the block handler alone does **not** prove the current `RootInjective` statement.
/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:5:There are two decisions before implementation. First, decide whether one block per `(parent, slot)` is the intended abstraction. This removes same-slot siblings that differ only in their supplied root. Second, decide whether to fix the current protocols first or to include a full-content codec for FG and the future proposer input. The second option has a larger proof and test cost.
/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:7:**Source scope and evidence.** All source paths below are relative to `/Users/francesco/ethereum/lean/available-chain`. The initial HEAD was `0b8ea1676320138d7626b441ae615d30eea66d37`. `Catalog/Mono.lean` and `Catalog/Standard.lean` were then untracked. The other session committed them during this study: HEAD became `ba9dac9a73c0c6ca1c6d265c65a63bbb5354292a`, with a clean status. A hash comparison of the 341 copied source and document files found only `docs/catalog.lock` changed. The saved initial lock has 141 entries; the later lock has 199. At final review, HEAD was `9e0b6207f5ef2fd6174282494579e530a8c818ff`, with a clean status. The only additional source change was a group of field-order tests appended to `Catalog/Standard.lean`; the root-related definitions did not change. The final lock still has 199 entries. This study includes the new catalog source and that final review.
/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:9:The evidence is in [the source snapshot](scratch/r194/source/), [its SHA-256 manifest](scratch/r194/source-manifest.json), [the source status](scratch/r194/source-status.json), and [the final catalog lock](scratch/r194/final-source/docs/catalog.lock). The final Standard source is saved in [final-source](scratch/r194/final-source/). Line references use the initial saved source. This also protects the references from later edits on main.
/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:13:**The defect and the exact scope of the premise.** `Objects/Identifiers.lean:13–24` gives roots the type `BlockId`, with an unrestricted `Nat` value and a linear order. Genesis has root zero. `Objects/Blocks.lean:14` permits any root in `.node parent slot root`. There is no content check in the type.
/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:15:Grid CO constructs `s * (parent.root.value + 1)` at `Model/Protocol.lean:292`. SA aliases that proposer. SA-PC constructs the same value at `Model/Choice.lean:87`; L* does so at `Model/Protocol.lean:258`. Thus slot 4 on genesis and slot 2 on the slot-1 block both have root 4. Another arithmetic example is the chain of roots `1, 4, 15, 64`: a faulty slot-7 block with root 7 gives its honest slot-8 child root 64. These are structural examples of the collision; this study does not claim a compiled execution witness for each regime.
/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:17:The more direct attack needs no honest arithmetic collision. A faulty proposer can supply a non-genesis block with root zero, or two distinct blocks with the same arbitrary root. The present handlers do not compare the supplied root with any encoding. A known parent, a suitable time, and the existing authentication and slot conditions permit such blocks to enter a store.
/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:19:`Statements/Generic/Conditions.lean:17–31` defines a wider scope than stored blocks:
