/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:26:For example, after adding only a handler root check, deliver `.node .genesis 1 ⟨0⟩`. The handler rejects it, but `BlockInRun` still names it. Genesis is also in scope, so `RootInjective` is false. Keeping the old `wellFormed` allows this example even under the wire portion of `ExecutionValid`. Moving the check only into `wellFormed` has the opposite defect: the engine calls `process` directly, so arbitrary raw event lists can still store malformed blocks. Both boundaries matter.
