/Users/francesco/ethereum/research/async-resilient-committees/tip-stability/codex/root-design.md:259:Some root reads use field names such as `entry`, `target`, or `lock`, with no literal `root` in the expression. Their semantic locations are `SimplexFG/Objects.NamedHeightPair.matchesEntry:24`; `Evidence.conflictsWithFinality:13`, `e1Fields:29`, `e2Fields:37`, and the evidence wrappers at `:47–113`; `Client.Record.with_target:39`, `with_lock:49`, `finality_pair:81`, `own_lock:90`, `height_pair:106`, `record_row:127`, and `createRow:147`. `KitFG/ClientSafety` proves these recorded-target and lock relations; `Certificates.RowWitnesses` and certificate extraction carry their values; `Provenance` links them to source and head roots. These are included by semantic inspection in addition to the lexical index.
